      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ferris built the \"Ellis House\" south of Manchester, where handmade bricks from his slaves earned it the nickname \"Brick Place\".",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellisville%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Vespasian Ellis, a newspaper editor, bought the house and later served as U.S. consul to Venezuela in 1842.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ellisville%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ellisville incorporated as a village in 1932 and became a city in 1957, yet its roots trace back to the early 1800s.",
